# Notation
#
# One record per symbol or symbol family. Every symbol a claim may use is
# declared here. Format is described in DATABASE.md.
#
#   writes      the symbol as it appears in a claim
#   reads       how a viewer says it in words
#   metamath    the set.mm syntax constructors the elaborator targets
#   first-used  the pilot that introduced it
#   note        anything a reader or an implementer needs
#
# A line beginning with # is a comment. A record begins at column 0 and its
# fields are indented.

notation number-systems
  writes      ℕ  ℕ₀  ℤ  ℚ  ℝ
  reads       the natural numbers, the natural numbers with zero, the integers,
              the rationals, the reals
  metamath    cn, cn0, cz, cq, cr
  first-used  sqrt2-irrational
  note        ℕ starts at 1, as set.mm's cn does, and ℕ₀ starts at 0. A reader
              taught that the natural numbers begin at 0 needs this pointer to
              say so. Nothing in any text assumes either convention beyond it.

notation relations
  writes      ∈  ∉  =  ≠  <  >  ≤  ≥
  reads       is in, is not in, equals, is not equal to, is less than,
              is greater than, is at most, is at least
  metamath    wcel, wnel, wceq, wne, clt, cle
  first-used  sqrt2-irrational

notation arithmetic-operations
  writes      +  −  ·  /  ²  ^  √
  reads       plus, minus, times, divided by, squared, to the power,
              the square root of
  metamath    caddc, cmin, cmul, cdiv, cexp, csqrt
  first-used  sqrt2-irrational
  note        Binary − and the general power ^ are used by the primes, Bezout,
              subsets, geometric series and intermediate value pilots and were
              declared in no pilot table. Added by the merge.

notation negation
  writes      −x
  reads       minus x
  metamath    cneg
  first-used  triangle-inequality
  note        Unary. Distinct from binary − in arithmetic-operations, which the
              parser will have to tell apart by position.

notation logical-symbols
  writes      ∀  ∃  ¬  ∧  ∨  →  ↔
  reads       for every, there is, not, and, or, implies, if and only if
  metamath    wal, wex, wn, wa, wo, wi, wb
  first-used  sqrt2-irrational
  note        SYNTAX.md writes ∀ ∃ ¬ ∧ ∨ as words in claims. Only → and ↔ are
              written as symbols, and the rest appear in database statements
              where words would be worse.

notation absolute-value
  writes      |x|
  reads       the absolute value of x
  metamath    cabs
  first-used  triangle-inequality
  note        Collides with cardinality and with distance. See DATABASE.md.

notation cardinality
  writes      |A|
  reads       the number of elements of A
  metamath    chash
  first-used  subsets
  note        Collides with absolute-value and with distance. See DATABASE.md.

notation distance
  writes      |PQ|
  reads       the distance from P to Q
  metamath    ( abs ` ( P − Q ) )
  first-used  isosceles
  note        Collides with absolute-value and with cardinality. See DATABASE.md.

notation factorial
  writes      n!
  reads       n factorial
  metamath    cfa
  first-used  infinitely-many-primes

notation gcd
  writes      gcd(a, b)
  reads       the greatest common divisor of a and b
  metamath    cgcd
  first-used  bezout

notation subset
  writes      ⊆
  reads       is a subset of
  metamath    wss
  first-used  bezout

notation set-operations
  writes      ∅  {a}  ∪  ∖  ∩
  reads       the empty set, the set whose only element is a, union, difference,
              intersection
  metamath    c0, csn, cun, cdif, cin
  first-used  subsets

notation powerset
  writes      𝒫A
  reads       the power set of A
  metamath    cpw
  first-used  cantor

notation set-builder
  writes      {t ∈ X : P(t)}
  reads       the set of t in X with P(t)
  metamath    crab
  first-used  bezout
  note        Told apart from set-image by what precedes the colon. See
              def:set-builder.

notation set-image
  writes      {E(s) : s ∈ Y}
  reads       the set of E(s) for s in Y
  metamath    cmpt, or crab with a witness
  first-used  subsets
  note        Told apart from set-builder by what precedes the colon. See
              def:set-image.

notation function
  writes      f : A → B,  f(x)
  reads       f is a function from A to B, f applied to x
  metamath    wf, cfv
  first-used  cantor
  note        The Cantor and intermediate value pilots wrote this row
              separately, the second as "f : D → ℝ". One row.

notation closed-interval
  writes      [a, b]
  reads       the closed interval from a to b
  metamath    cicc
  first-used  intermediate-value

notation point
  writes      point
  reads       a point of the plane
  metamath    an element of ℂ
  first-used  isosceles

notation angle
  writes      ∠PQR
  reads       the angle at Q from P to R
  metamath    ( ( P − Q ) F ( R − Q ) ), with F the angle function
  first-used  isosceles
  note        set.mm's angle function is signed. See def:angle.

notation congruent
  writes      triangle PQR ≅ triangle P′Q′R′
  reads       triangle PQR is congruent to triangle P′Q′R′
  metamath    none
  first-used  isosceles

notation sum-function
  writes      S(n)
  reads       the sum of the first n natural numbers
  metamath    Σ k ∈ (1...n) k
  first-used  sum-formula
  note        Introduced by def:S, which is local to the sum-formula pilot.

notation geometric-function
  writes      G(n)
  reads       the sum of the first n + 1 powers of a
  metamath    Σ k ∈ (0...n) a^k
  first-used  geometric-series
  note        Introduced by def:G, which is local to the geometric-series pilot.
